# Authentication & User System — Implementation Spec

**Scope:** Register, Login, Forgot/Reset Password, Email Verification (link-based, no OTP), User Management, Roles, XP, Badges, Memory.
**Explicitly out of scope for now:** OTP, OAuth/social login.

---

## 1. Locked Tech Decisions

| Layer | Choice | Why |
|---|---|---|
| Backend | Node.js + Express | Matches Next.js frontend — one language across the team |
| ORM | Prisma | Type-safe, auto-migrations, works great with Postgres |
| Database | PostgreSQL | Relational integrity for users/roles/tokens; JSONB where flexibility is needed |
| Password hashing | bcrypt (cost factor 12) | Industry standard, simple, no external dependency |
| Auth tokens | JWT access token + opaque refresh token | Access token stateless & short-lived; refresh token stored & revocable |
| Refresh token storage | httpOnly, secure, sameSite=strict cookie | Not accessible to JS → mitigates XSS token theft |
| Email delivery | Nodemailer (SMTP) | Works with any SMTP provider (Gmail, etc.) — no vendor lock-in |
| Validation | Zod | Type-safe schema validation on every request body |
| Rate limiting | express-rate-limit + Redis store (or in-memory if no Redis yet) | Stops brute force on login/register/reset |
| Security headers | Helmet | One-line baseline hardening |
| File uploads | Cloudinary + Multer | Server-side image upload, CDN delivery, on-the-fly transformations |
| Image middleware | Multer (memory storage) | Parses multipart form, 5 MB limit, image-only filter |

No OTP = email verification and password reset both use a **signed, single-use link with an expiring token**, not a code.

